# IVI3D printer main board - A33 Linux UART documentation log
# Prepared 2026-11-07 (America/Chicago, CST = UTC-6) from saved Mac captures in /tmp/ivi_uart_capture
# FORMAT: raw cleaned/redacted UART transcript lines are UNCOMMENTED. Lines starting "# " are documentation.
# "# NOTE:" explains the next transcript line(s); "# COMMAND:" explains a command sent and how to read its response.
# ">>>CMD <text>" lines are markers written by the Mac capture script when it transmitted <text>; the board echo follows.
# Board clock = UTC. Mac status files = CST.
# Redacted: serial numbers, eMMC/card serials, UUIDs, MAC/BSSID, SSIDs, IP addresses, netmasks, personal paths.
# No raw firmware contents included. Scope: A33 Linux side only. No SWD/STM32/GD32 access was performed.
#
# ==============================================================================
# 1. SOURCE MANIFEST
# ==============================================================================
#   - boot3_115200_20261107_153612.bin: clean cold boot, receive-only, 115200 8N1 (selected representative boot)
#   - boot5_115200_20261107_161435.bin(+.status): clean boot + single CR -> "# " prompt test
#   - shell_ro_20261107_161716.log: first read-only shell inspection (id/uname/proc/sys)
#   - sdinsert_115200_20261107_162100.bin: receive-only monitor during live microSD insertion
#   - sd_ro_20261107_162419.log: read-only SD metadata session (start contaminated by host replay; see note)
#   - cont_20261107_163524.bin(+.status): continuous session: boot + card guard + 64 KiB dd read test
#   - backup_20261107_164205.bin(+.status): continuous session: boot + SD-card backup of eMMC + verify + unmount
#   - agent session transcript: Mac-side md5 verification of the 14TB copy (quoted from recorded tool output)
# Omitted as INVALID (host-side CP2102/macOS replay artifact, repeated stale data at impossible rate):
#   boot_115200_20261107_153330.bin, boot2_115200_20261107_153447.bin, backup_20261107_164058.bin,
#   sanity2_*.bin (16:30), sd_dd_20261107_163308.log. Duplicate clean boots (boot5/cont/backup) not repeated in full.
#
# ==============================================================================
# 2. CHRONOLOGY (CST)
# ==============================================================================
#   - 15:31 18 s receive-only capture at 115200 8N1 (hypothesis) -> readable Marlin-style poll text: baud confirmed
#   - 15:33-15:35 two captures invalid: same lines replayed at >200 KB/s (impossible at 115200); stopped
#   - 15:36 board off, 0-byte quiet check; 15:36:12 capture armed; user powered on -> full clean boot (boot3)
#   - 16:14:35 capture armed with board off; boot; 16:15:45 exactly one CR sent -> "# " root shell prompt
#   - 16:17 bounded read-only shell inspection (id, uname, /proc, /sys)
#   - 16:21 receive-only monitor; user inserted 8 GB microSD -> mmcblk1 detected, one -123 read error at insert
#   - 16:24 read-only SD metadata (session start contaminated by replay; board executed id once)
#   - 16:30/16:33 sanity checks failed (replay) -> no commands sent
#   - 16:35:24 armed with board off; boot; 16:36:36 card test: dd of last 64 KiB OK (DD_RC=0)
#   - 16:40:58 arm aborted (replay even with board off -> host-side); adapter replugged
#   - 16:42:05 armed; boot; 16:43:58-16:54:39 backup to SD; 16:56-17:00 md5sum -c OK; 17:00:54 SD unmounted; reader closed
#   - 17:39 user copied folder to 14TB; Mac md5 verification: all 3 images match
#
# ==============================================================================
# 3. REPRESENTATIVE CLEAN COLD BOOT (boot0 -> U-Boot -> Linux -> app)
# ==============================================================================
# Source boot3_115200_20261107_153612.bin; receive-only, nothing transmitted. Output: boot0/U-Boot/Linux/app (mixed console).
# Leading line noise before "BOOT0" removed.
